## Resumo das Decisões de Design

| Decisão | Alternativa Rejeitada | Motivo |
|---------|----------------------|--------|
| Array em memória | Banco de dados | Simplicidade educacional, zero configuração |
| Classes de erro customizadas | Strings genéricas | Tratamento granular por tipo, stack trace preservado |
| PUT (substituição) | PATCH (parcial) | Mais simples de implementar e demonstrar |
| try/catch em rotas | Express 5 async catch | Compatibilidade com Express 4 |
| Arquivos separados | Monolito único | Manutenibilidade, testabilidade, escalabilidade |
| Query params para filtro | Parâmetros de rota | Opcionalidade, combinações livres, padrão REST |

# REST API for Book Management — Complete Implementation

## Overview

This project implements a fully functional RESTful API for managing books using **Node.js** and **Express.js**. The API supports all standard CRUD operations (Create, Read, Update, Delete) plus an analytics endpoint for statistics. It uses **in-memory storage** (an array of objects) so no external database is required — ideal for learning and prototyping.

Key design decisions:
- **REST conventions**: Resource-based URLs (`/books`, `/books/:id`), proper HTTP methods, and status codes.
- **Async/Await pattern**: All route handlers are async to model real-world database interactions and prevent blocking the event loop.
- **Custom error classes**: Three distinct error types (`NotFoundError`, `ValidationError`, `InternalServerError`) enable precise client-side handling.
- **Centralized error middleware**: A single Express error-handling middleware catches all errors and returns consistent JSON responses.
- **Input validation**: Every create/update request is validated before processing to prevent malformed data.
- **JSDoc documentation**: Every function, parameter, and endpoint is fully documented for maintainability.

