## Overview

This project demonstrates how to build a simple but production‑ready REST API using Node.js and Express.js.  
We store books in an in‑memory array (no database) so the code stays focused on routing, validation, error handling, and statistics.  
Each HTTP method maps to a CRUD operation:

| Method | Endpoint        | Purpose                     |
|--------|-----------------|-----------------------------|
| GET    | /books          | List all books (with filters) |
| GET    | /books/:id      | Get one book by ID            |
| POST   | /books          | Create a new book             |
| PUT    | /books/:id      | Update an existing book       |
| DELETE | /books/:id      | Delete a book                 |
| GET    | /stats          | Return aggregate statistics   |

We also include:

- Custom `AppError` class for consistent error responses.
- Global error‑handling middleware that catches synchronous and asynchronous errors.
- Input validation with clear 400‑level error messages.
- JSDoc comments on every exported function and route handler.
- A README.md with setup instructions and curl examples.

